.Dd November 15, 2026
.Dt WLCOMPD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm wlcompd
.Nd Wayland compositor for the framebuffer
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar font
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
daemon is the Wayland compositor of Ixolo.
It draws on the framebuffer
.Pa /dev/fb0
and takes input from the keyboard and the mouse.
Wayland clients connect to it over a
.Ux Ns -domain
socket and hand it their pixels in shared memory.
.Pp
The optional
.Ar font
argument is the path of a TrueType font used for window titles.
The default is
.Pa /usr/share/fonts/TTF/DejaVuSans.ttf .
If the font cannot be loaded,
.Nm
prints a warning and runs without title text.
.Pp
.Nm
does not detach from the terminal.
It runs until it is killed.
.Ss Protocols
.Nm
implements these Wayland globals:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Li wl_compositor , wl_subcompositor , wl_shm
Surfaces, subsurfaces and shared-memory buffers.
Only
.Li wl_shm
buffers are accepted.
A buffer may be at most 4096 by 4096 pixels.
.It Li wl_seat
One seat, named
.Dq minix-seat0 ,
with a pointer and a keyboard.
.It Li wl_output
One output, the size of the framebuffer, at a refresh rate of 60 Hz.
Its make is
.Dq Ixolo
and its model is
.Dq fb0 .
.It Li wl_data_device_manager
Accepted, but see
.Sx BUGS .
.It Li xdg_wm_base
Toplevel windows and popups (xdg-shell).
.It Li zwlr_layer_shell_v1
Panels, docks and backgrounds that anchor to an edge of the screen.
.It Li zwlr_foreign_toplevel_manager_v1
Lets a taskbar list, activate, minimize, maximize and close windows.
.It Li ext_workspace_manager_v1
Lets a pager list and switch virtual desktops.
.It Li zxdg_decoration_manager_v1
Every request is answered with server-side decorations.
.El
.Ss Windows
.Nm
draws a title bar above each toplevel window.
The title bar shows the window title and a close box marked
.Sq x
at its right end.
A small resize grip is drawn in the bottom-right corner of the window.
.Pp
New windows open at staggered positions near the top-left corner.
A window that is nearly as large as the screen is moved so that its
title bar stays on screen.
.Ss Mouse
Only the left mouse button is used.
.Bl -bullet
.It
A click on a window raises it and gives it keyboard focus.
.It
Dragging the title bar moves the window.
.It
A click on the close box asks the client to close the window.
The client may refuse.
.It
Dragging the resize grip asks the client to resize the window.
The smallest size is 80 by 48 pixels.
.It
A click anywhere outside an open popup dismisses the popup.
.It
A click on a layer-shell surface that asked for keyboard interactivity
gives it keyboard focus.
.El
.Pp
If a client does not set its own cursor,
.Nm
draws a white arrow.
.Ss Keyboard
Every key is passed to the window that has keyboard focus.
.Nm
has no keyboard shortcuts of its own.
Keys are translated with the XKB keymap in
.Pa /usr/share/xkb/us.xkb ,
which is also sent to each client.
If the keymap cannot be loaded, clients are told there is no keymap.
Clients are told to repeat keys 25 times a second after a delay of
400 milliseconds.
.Ss Virtual desktops
There are four virtual desktops, named
.Dq 1
to
.Dq 4 .
A new window opens on the current desktop.
Panels and other layer-shell surfaces appear on every desktop.
Desktops can only be switched by a client, such as a panel pager,
through the ext-workspace protocol.
Clients cannot create or remove desktops.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
.It Ev XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
The directory in which the listening socket is created.
It must be set to an absolute path, or
.Nm
exits.
.El
.Pp
.Nm
creates the first free socket named
.Pa wayland-0
to
.Pa wayland-32
in that directory, with a
.Pa .lock
file beside it.
The chosen name is printed when the compositor is ready.
Clients find it through
.Ev WAYLAND_DISPLAY ,
which defaults to
.Pa wayland-0 .
.Nm
does not set
.Ev WAYLAND_DISPLAY
itself.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /usr/share/fonts/TTF/DejaVuSans.ttf -compact
.It Pa /dev/fb0
The framebuffer.
.It Pa /dev/kbdmux
The keyboard.
.Pa /dev/kbd0
is tried if it cannot be opened.
.It Pa /dev/mousemux
The mouse.
.Pa /dev/mouse0
is tried if it cannot be opened.
.It Pa /usr/share/xkb/us.xkb
The keyboard map.
.It Pa /usr/share/fonts/TTF/DejaVuSans.ttf
The default title font.
.It Pa /tmp/wlcompd-keymap. Ns Ar XXXXXX
A copy of the keymap, passed to clients as a file descriptor.
It is unlinked as soon as it is created.
.It Pa /etc/rc.d/wlcompd
Starts
.Nm
at boot when
.Va wlcompd
is set to
.Dq YES
in
.Xr rc.conf 5 .
The script sets
.Ev XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
to
.Pa /var/run
if it is unset, and records the process ID in
.Pa /var/run/wlcompd.pid .
.It Pa /var/log/wlcompd.log
Where the boot script sends the output of
.Nm .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 1 if it cannot open the framebuffer, set up the Wayland display or
create its listening socket.
Once it is running it does not exit by itself.
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Nm
logs its activity to standard output.
When start-up is complete it prints a line beginning with
.Dq WLCOMPD READY ,
which gives the framebuffer size, the socket name and whether a mouse,
a keyboard and a keymap were found.
For every committed buffer it prints a checksum of the pixels;
.Xr wlclient 1
prints the matching checksum on its side.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr wlclient 1 ,
.Xr wlcoreprobe 1 ,
.Xr wlprobe 1 ,
.Xr rc.conf 5 ,
.Xr fbcompd 8 ,
.Xr minix-service 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
daemon first appeared in Ixolo 0.1.
.Sh CAVEATS
.Nm
and
.Xr fbcompd 8
must not run at the same time.
Both use the framebuffer and the keyboard.
.Pp
While
.Nm
holds
.Pa /dev/kbdmux ,
the console no longer receives keyboard input.
.Sh BUGS
Only the left mouse button is reported to clients.
There are no scroll wheel and no touch events.
.Pp
The clipboard owner is recorded, but other clients are never offered
the data, so paste between clients does not work.
Drag and drop is accepted and ignored.
.Pp
Requests from a client to maximize, minimize or fullscreen its own
window are ignored.
A window can be maximized or minimized only through
.Li zwlr_foreign_toplevel_manager_v1 .
Fullscreen through that protocol is treated as maximize.
.Pp
Windows cannot be moved to another virtual desktop.
.Pp
The exclusive zone of a panel is recorded but not applied:
windows may sit underneath a panel.
.Pp
Popup constraint adjustment, input regions and opaque regions are
ignored.
.Pp
Window titles are cut to 63 bytes.
